  "sevenDays": "Seven days of scores cannot validate a direction call: the confidence interval on a seven day hit rate is plus or minus 37 points. The recommendations do not come from the daily predictions. They come from rules with decades of evidence: a trend filter, 12-1 momentum, inverse vol sizing to a sleeve vol target (25% ETFs, 50% stocks), and VIX term structure risk off.",
  "direction": "Daily direction is close to a coin flip in every honest study. The daily forecast is a full density (mean, sigma, probability up, conformal band) scored every day against a random walk with drift and against climatology. Volatility has real measurable skill; direction mostly does not, and the scorecard says which is which.",
